<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Leer buys Dutch paper depot.</title>
<headline>Van Leer buys Dutch paper depot.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch packaging group Van Leer said on Monday it was planning to buy a waste paper depot in the Dutch city Groningen from KNP BT.</p>
<p>&quot;LeoReitsma BV, unit of Van Leer NV, and KNP Paper Recycling BV, unit of KNP BT, have signed an agreement that LeoReitsma acquires the assets of the depot Marum (Groningen) of KNP BT Paper Recycling,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>No financial details were given on the deal.</p>
<p>The depot in Groningen employs 15 staff.</p>
<p>Van Leer is one of the world's largest packaging companies with 140 operating companies in 42 countries.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
